 ```
 
+#### Max Consecutive Losses
+
+`MaxConsecutiveLosses` counts losing trades (any trade that closed with a negative profit, regardless of exit reason) for a pair, starting from the most recent trade and going backwards. As soon as a trade that did not lose money is encountered, the streak is broken.
+
+If `trade_limit` or more losing trades occurred in a row (within `lookback_period` in minutes, or in candles when using `lookback_period_candles`) trading will stop for that pair for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`).
+
+This applies per pair by default, and additionally across all pairs (bot-wide) unless `only_per_pair` is set to true. To get both a per-pair and a bot-wide guard, configure `MaxConsecutiveLosses` twice - once with `only_per_pair: true`, and once without.
+
+Similarly to `StoplossGuard`, setting `only_per_side` will make the bot only consider one side (long/short) of trades, allowing for example shorts to continue after a losing streak of longs.
+
+The below example stops trading a pair for 12 candles after 4 losing trades occurred in a row for that pair within the last 24 candles, and additionally stops trading for all pairs for 4 candles after 6 losing trades occurred in a row bot-wide within the last 24 candles.
+
+``` python
+@property
+def protections(self):
+    return [
+        {
+            "method": "MaxConsecutiveLosses",
+            "lookback_period_candles": 24,
+            "trade_limit": 4,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 12,
+            "only_per_pair": True,
+        },
+        {
+            "method": "MaxConsecutiveLosses",
+            "lookback_period_candles": 24,
+            "trade_limit": 6,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 4,
+            "only_per_pair": False,
+        },
+    ]
+```
+
+Once the cooldown period elapses, new trades for the affected pair(s) are automatically allowed again - no manual intervention is required. As with all protections, triggering a lock is broadcast through the same notification channel used for other automatic pauses (e.g. Telegram / webhook `protection_trigger` and `protection_trigger_global` messages).
+
 #### Cooldown Period
 
 `CooldownPeriod` locks a pair for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`) after exiting, avoiding a re-entry for this pair for `stop_duration` minutes.
